<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 28 July, from 1148 to 1932.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/damascus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/damascus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1148 CE <span class="tih-ago">878 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The crusader siege of Damascus ends in failure</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> by the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vii-of-france">Louis VII of France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-iii-of-germany">Conrad III of Germany</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> failed after four days. The Muslim victory led to the disintegration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1402">1402 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">624 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Timur defeats and captures Sultan Bayezid I at Ankara</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the Çubuk plain near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> won a crushing victory over the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a>, who was captured and died in captivity. The defeat plunged the Ottoman state into civil war, the Ottoman Interregnum.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ankara">Battle of Ankara</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1540">1540 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">486 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Cromwell is beheaded on Tower Hill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s chief minister, architect of the break with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the Dissolution of the Monasteries, was executed for treason and heresy. His fall followed the king's disastrous marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-cleves">Anne of Cleves</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1656">1656 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">370 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Warsaw begins in the Second Northern War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> began a battle against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> that lasted until 30 July. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajo">Hajo</a> Holborn, this major clash of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-northern-war">Second Northern War</a> marked the beginning of Prussian military history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-northern-war">Second Northern War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1750">1750 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">276 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Johann Sebastian Bach dies in Leipzig</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bach died aged 65 after failed eye operations. Little valued by his immediate successors, his music was revived in the nineteenth century, and he is now ranked among the greatest composers.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1868">1868 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">158 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The 14th Amendment is certified as part of the US Constitution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretary of State William Seward certified the 14th Amendment, guaranteeing citizenship and equal protection of the laws. It became the basis for many landmark civil rights rulings.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1914">1914 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Austria-Hungary declares war on Serbia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">One month after the assassination of Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria">Franz Ferdinand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>. Within a week <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> were drawn in, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> had begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1932">1932 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">94 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US troops drive the Bonus Army out of Washington</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On Hoover's orders, troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douglas-macarthur">Douglas MacArthur</a> used tear gas and bayonets to clear camps of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> veterans demanding early payment of bonuses. The scenes damaged Hoover's re-election hopes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 28 July <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-duke-of-julich-cleves-berg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-duke-of-julich-cleves-berg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William, Duke of Jülich-Cleves-Berg</span><span class="tp">1516–1592</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-sarraut"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-sarraut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert Sarraut</span><span class="tp">1872–1962</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vajiralongkorn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vajiralongkorn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vajiralongkorn</span><span class="tp">b. 1952</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hugo-chavez"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hugo-chavez.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hugo Chávez</span><span class="tp">1954–2013</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
